curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-{x}^{2} & =x+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+x-2 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$-2\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/aab6fb99694b518bfa9d200a75876c9e888ba1ab7d699464bc9caca360be775a.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 1,\\,x+1\\le y\\le 3-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-81340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{3-{x}^{2}}^{x+1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{