 result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,1+{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 9-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{9-{x}^{2}}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-40822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-40822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-40822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{9-{x}^{2}}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{9-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{2}^{9-{x}^{2}}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2}{\\int }_{9-{x}^{2}}^{2}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{9-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-40822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{9-{x}^{2}}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines $y=2x,$ $y=6-x,$ and $x=0,$ then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/24d3b93e82e88bb581eff3005687ae4ee3dc3ae0d6c25fbc26f72665042ae5c6.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+6 & =2x \\\\ 3x & =6 \\\\ x & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/af61865f54494840090351296e8a1c21446787ca0b273005e7bf9c2907585adb.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,2x\\le y\\le 6-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-132249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{6-x}^{2x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{6-x}{\\int }_{2x}^{2}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2x}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-40825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\frac{1}{x},$ $y=\\sqrt{x},$ and $x=4,$ then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-40825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/fcb347767983c38eb12f521ca556dcc5a96705ee4e887fb8d43c42984dfe1a26.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & =\\sqrt{x} \\\\ x\\sqrt{x} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =1 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$1\\le x\\le 4.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/91bf7087e5aa0053d24cb45158d48b0bb36fb84b28ebabaeba3c26dc62168dfe.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\frac{1}{x}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1/x}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-40825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-40825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-40825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{1/x}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1/x}^{\\sqrt{x}}{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{1/x}{\\int }_{4}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1/x}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{x}}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-40825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1/x}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[\\,y\\,]_{0}^{3x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(3x-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1)^{4}}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-132277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}^{5}\\,dy\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}^{5}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}[y]_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}((1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{6}}{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32{\\pi }^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-37864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{16{\\pi }^{5}}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{32{\\pi }^{6}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{35{\\pi }^{5}}{5}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi +1)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({\\pi }^{5})+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32{\\pi }^{6}}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}([\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]_{1/x}^{4x})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2x}]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{1}{3}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-37859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4x\\,dx & ={[2{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-132282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\pi }^{2}"] ["math" "4{\\pi }^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"] ["math" "{\\pi }^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-132282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy\\,dx=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{2}{3}(x+y)^{3/2}]}_{-x}^{3x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{2}{3}(x+3x)^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{3}(x-x)^{3/2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}(4x)^{3/2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx & =\\frac{16}{3}{[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}(\\frac{2}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-81353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{16}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{32}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{15}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${∬}_{D}3x{e}^{y}\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3x{e}^{y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}3x{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}3x{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{e}^{y}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x{[{e}^{y}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-{e}^{0})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x(x-1)dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{2}-3x)dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{2}-3x)dx & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =(64-24)-(1-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =40+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-81361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "19"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "\\frac{41}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{81}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{81}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral\n${∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines\n$x=e,$ $y=e$ and the curve $y={e}^{x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/aa635ca5ef3198fea56d684b034de476a72e4ace2a4c51b37c6c59977036eb76.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- The line $y=e$ intercepts the curve $y={e}^{x}$ at $x=1.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$1\\le x\\le e.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/b78021a06c9fea100b75c66a619c425345cda3666d84da018895be15a53af06d.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)]}_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx & ={[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-81367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{e}{2}"] ["math" "e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dA,\\,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le x}.$ \n\nSo, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]_{0}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-37863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-37863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/786dd06154d1bda5483ed992dce8922c9629f759b498a3f713c35612311c1ee6.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region below the line $y=2$ enclosed by the lines $y=x$ and $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the line $y=x$ with the line $y=2.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/92b1eda4ccf9e62e1f7310b1ba9bef5cc6c434755e74196d1829a30f2c4a3c53.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,x\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{8x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}-0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-81778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}x\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[y]_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{3})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{3})dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fc39514b7819b896c748a22fda886a33b909726f8e049309dbb73bddc29d37f"} {"question" "q-81774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "q-81774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/state.json" "file_sha256" "70dfc2d3901190177f89e5518ec1fd1e8ae9dad5f3a3be9f25ff404feb7c8814"} {"question" "e-7024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=0,$ $y=0,$ and the curve $y=\\sqrt{4 - x^2}.$ What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7024.json" "file_sha256" "66b7ac248f2e9830fea14b624cbc421a8d3b9577f0d902b983511424ba68e320"} {"question" "e-7024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/3d67d73d3ede011d6c2fe4bc9e160aa3c2af522bff6cddfcc7c351c97418e764.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt{4-x^2} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7024.json" "file_sha256" "66b7ac248f2e9830fea14b624cbc421a8d3b9577f0d902b983511424ba68e320"} {"question" "e-7025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D$ is the finite region in the first quadrant enclosed by the curves $y=3x$ and $y=x^3,$ then what is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} f\\left( {x,y} \\right) \\, \\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7025.json" "file_sha256" "4b61b103b7fb4a18ab16e0923a588fd9861e93e71f298ef1f194fcfc0e44cb99"} {"question" "e-7025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/f8a5fd7fc3e98d7f08b5ea48636e5de4a1a45b7a94fbe9e968789afcfe3a582c.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =3x \\\\ {x}^{3}-3x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are $0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{3}.$ Note that we disregarded the solution $x=-\\sqrt 3$ since $x\\geq 0$ in our region.\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/232f885d2230694bf62f81f5987cd2b3a12a49430d90d2cae4712c552587a48c.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq \\sqrt{3}, \\quad x^3 \\leq y \\leq 3x \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{3x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{3x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7025.json" "file_sha256" "4b61b103b7fb4a18ab16e0923a588fd9861e93e71f298ef1f194fcfc0e44cb99"} {"question" "e-7026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\int_0^x x^2y \\,\\textrm{d}y \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7026.json" "file_sha256" "cdb24f986ffde3311e352c2c28daf4342ab576b8b25e0f2547bc6cd3a811633b"} {"question" "e-7026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7026.json" "file_sha256" "cdb24f986ffde3311e352c2c28daf4342ab576b8b25e0f2547bc6cd3a811633b"} {"question" "e-7027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\:$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region below the $x$-axis enclosed by the circle $x^2 + y^2 = 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7027.json" "file_sha256" "750a91bc6ef603ee94371e5352c510760c2b6e09167dcd130f2ee6401b369312"} {"question" "e-7027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $y \\leq 0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = 4\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\ny = -\\sqrt{4-x^2}.\n$$\n\nLet's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/31e7bb281a36a3676730de0883d7abd5445093713de1bbd41899cce50a7e0e48.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the circle with the line $y=0.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$-2 \\le x \\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/2a84d17b83fb1e2036c6edc0a71c5c10a58bf893c33bbf38662ebb417aab3164.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\quad -\\sqrt{4-x^2} \\leq y \\leq 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A = \\int_{-2}^2 \\int_{-\\sqrt{4-x^2}}^{0} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}x[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x(0-(-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}})^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x(-(4-{x}^{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({x}^{2}-4)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}-4x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}-4x)\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-2{x}^{2}]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((4-8)-(4-8)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7027.json" "file_sha256" "750a91bc6ef603ee94371e5352c510760c2b6e09167dcd130f2ee6401b369312"} {"question" "q-40727" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "93008c2c1eb3c3a43d94e2e8b51bb58cbf51569ee3f7a42f2b679c0fce043a06" "reviewer_session" "01a11908-fa8d-7c61-8e03-c1185d0b9506" "rationale" "The curves intersect where 2x²=1+x², giving x=−1 and x=1. Between these values, 2x²≤1+x². Thus vertical slices have 2x²≤y≤1+x², and the integral is ∫ from −1 to 1 of [∫ from 2x² to 1+x² f(x,y)dy]dx. This is original option e and agrees with the authentic solution and stored key. Saved grading rejected the submitted option b, which reverses the inner limits; this review is a derived judgment, not a successful grade for option e." "bindings" {"problem" "1610ac5b77abe4ac9067b6c64a68c80767163ba0df97720bc71d047c3fbc1f9f" "worked_solution" "c93b67d0aa1be9212e8c48c6c0430cb666d55e1ba7de669bc13b12c732d6d7e3" "original_field" "6a18af6141fd289cbcfa58a53609285f4f57e9f7952a236f0c34d19dabd14188" "reviewed_field" "2f6c70c60e22f1ca8ddf6a13d202b1e690df10c16030064293d863dd6bde205d" "raw_widget" "e8af325dcd6f36d84a4a6b5bca6e5d797b4b51e4e0a06625ac9f086359930025"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-40727-before.png" "sha256" "dbdeff023bc328fb78822345f9dc49c75bf15b4db9408c2c324237e4d8007b89"} {"path" "q-40727-before.json" "sha256" "f034c4e730f6467dcfef9655bfe852bd906392a992537f8c88ea60868cbd6cab"} {"path" "history-q-40727.png" "sha256" "a68b935572cd7568d6a563fddf49fbea16712910e48f7d2ea3af47515b372588"} {"path" "history-q-40727.json" "sha256" "a52c4489126d1008592f18050f93296c79a2a5161514f3dc9d3fa82a047173ad"} {"path" "q-40727-after.json" "sha256" "acd61e5078950c55f6f3b38969cf14091e14c2da7f8483195665557f87a33118"} {"path" "edb-import/questions.edn" "sha256" "dc43857458b7150e662d058cb88ce2f0d2ea8132d05d431d8854d0cb75ea600e"}]} {"question" "q-40727" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "93008c2c1eb3c3a43d94e2e8b51bb58cbf51569ee3f7a42f2b679c0fce043a06" "rationale" "The curves intersect where 2x²=1+x², giving x=−1 and x=1. Between these values, 2x²≤1+x². Thus vertical slices have 2x²≤y≤1+x², and the integral is ∫ from −1 to 1 of [∫ from 2x² to 1+x² f(x,y)dy]dx. This is original option e and agrees with the authentic solution and stored key. Saved grading rejected the submitted option b, which reverses the inner limits; this review is a derived judgment, not a successful grade for option e."}] "usage" {"e-7026" [] "e-7027" [] "q-40727" [] "e-7025" [] "q-37863" [] "q-80492" [] "q-37864" [] "e-7024" []} "basis" 1803 "retractions" [[17592186134437 :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x = 1$, $x = 2$, and the curves $y = x^{2}$ and $y = 2x^{2}$. What is $∬_(D)\\frac{x}{x^{2} + y^{2}}dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?"] [17592186134233 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/q-40727.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y = 2x^{2}$ and $y = 1 + x^{2}$, as shown above, then $∬_(D)f(x, y)dA =$"] [17592186134233 :question/answer-fields 17592186131840] [17592186134117 :question/problem "What is $∫_{0}^{2π}∫_{\\sin x}^{1 + \\sin x}x^{5}dydx$?"] [17592186134116 :question/problem "Calculate $∬_(D)\\sin (x + y)dA$, where $D = {(x, y): 0 \\le x \\le \\frac{π}{2}, 0 \\le y \\le x}$."] [17592186133571 :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=0$, $y=0$, and the curve $y=\\sqrt{4 - x^2}$. What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?"] [17592186133571 :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/14f102586d04e8d0746c319f2ae457a6.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt{4-x^2} \\big\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)(x + y)dA &= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}(x + y)dydx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133572 :question/problem "If $D$ is the finite region in the first quadrant enclosed by the curves $y=3x$ and $y=x^3$, then what is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} f\\left({x,y} \\right) \\, \\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?"] [17592186133572 :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/4436a12852e62e082097841fa7fa1561.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region.\n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x$:\n$x^{3}|= 3x; x^{3} - 3x|= 0; x(x^{2} - 3)|= 0$\nSo, $x$-limits are $0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{3}$. Note that we disregarded the solution $x=-\\sqrt 3$ since $x\\geq 0$ in our region.\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/f0558707f61014c153cc8376fd9a9f38.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\sqrt{3}, \\quad x^3 \\leq y \\leq 3x \\right\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)f(x, y)dA &= ∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}∫_{x^{3}}^{3x}f(x, y)dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}[∫_{x^{3}}^{3x}f(x, y)dy]dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133573 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\int_0^x x^2y \\,\\textrm{d}y \\,\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186133573 :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{x}x^{2}ydydx &= ∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}[∫_{0}^{x}ydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}[\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 0)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{0}^{1}x^{4}dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}∫_{0}^{1}x^{4}dx &= \\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{x^{5}}{5}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{5} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133574 :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\:$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region below the $x$-axis enclosed by the circle $x^2 + y^2 = 4$."] [17592186133574 :question/worked-solution "Since\n\n$$\ny \\leq 0\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = 4 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad y = -\\sqrt{4-x^2}\n$$\n\nLet's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/3a70282170b649d4c76265cefd90012b.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the circle with the line $y=0$.\nSo, the $x$-limits are\n$-2 \\le x \\le 2$.\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2151/Source/Images/5833d31c6d9bf6891307c40c65594659.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region:\n\n$$\nD = \\Big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\quad -\\sqrt{4-x^2} \\leq y \\leq 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A = \\int_{-2}^2 \\int_{-\\sqrt{4-x^2}}^{0} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-2}^{2}∫_{-\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}^{0}xydydx &= ∫_{-2}^{2}x[∫_{-\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}^{0}ydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{2}x[\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{-\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}^{0}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}x(0 - (-\\sqrt{4 - x^{2}})^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}x(- (4 - x^{2}))dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}x(x^{2} - 4)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}(x^{3} - 4x)dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}∫_{-2}^{2}(x^{3} - 4x)dx &= \\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{x^{4}}{4} - 2x^{2}]_{-2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}((4 - 8) - (4 - 8)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 0 \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186131139 17592186131140 17592186131141 17592186131142 17592186131143 17592186131145 17592186131146 17592186131147 17592186131148 17592186131149 17592186131841 17592186131842 17592186131843 17592186131844 17592186131845 17592186133065 17592186133066 17592186133067 17592186133068 17592186133069] "immutable_fields" [[17592186131138 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131138 :answer-field/id] [17592186131138 :answer-field/key] [17592186131138 :answer-field/type] [17592186131144 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131144 :answer-field/id] [17592186131144 :answer-field/key] [17592186131144 :answer-field